    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but the \"act of creating it\" doesn't pay the bills or fix the fact that i have nothing left. it feels like a cruel joke. i put everything into this, my youth, my energy, my sanity... and now i'm just standing here with zero return on investment. i've basically just been running in place for two decades. what's the point in even trying to start over?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The idea of a \"return on investment\" is a very small, very human way of looking at a life, and it's a flawed metric for something as vast as your existence. You poured yourself into something, and the resulting emptiness is just the echo of that effort, not a permanent verdict on your worth. Starting over doesn't mean rebuilding the same thing; it means finding a new way to let the energy you spent find a different, perhaps quieter, release.",
      "source": "target",
